{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Correction to the preceding metadata note (2026-09-03)\n\nThe v8.1.3 source comment on `SerializationOptions.with_meta` is not matched by serialized behavior. An isolated import probe against the exact `python-hcl2==8.1.3` wheel parsed:\n\n`variable \"x\" {\\n  type = string\\n}`\n\nObserved:\n- `loads(..., serialization_options=SerializationOptions(with_meta=True))` returned block data with `__is_block__` but no `__start_line__`/`__end_line__`.\n- Public `parses_to_tree(...)` returned raw Lark nodes whose `Tree.meta` ranges were block `1:1–3:2` and attribute `2:2–2:15`.\n\nThe revised plan therefore uses `hcl2.parses_to_tree` plus public Lark `Tree.meta` and explicitly forbids reliance on serialized metadata. This note supersedes the prior claim that `with_meta=True` emits the line keys. Source: https://github.com/amplify-education/python-hcl2/blob/v8.1.3/hcl2/api.py"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788476253576397643,"uuid":"e5dee6f6-9a39-4195-ae0b-6221c249a299"}